      "note": "Inspected owner-supplied carolina-elementary-school.png on 2026-10-08; capture date unknown. URL locates the site. Hand re-traced on 2026-10-08 from the owner image at enlarged scale: every distinguishable crown, canopy belt, lawn, planted bed, garden plot, hedge, path, apron, court and parking area is traced where the image shows it, and bare ground stays bare. Re-registered by hand (similarity fit, checks 1.3Ã¢â‚¬â€œ2.5 m). The west half of the central yard is patchy dry turf (grass); its east half is worn orange soil and stays bare. The gate walk from Panicuason Road along the white-walled stage enclosure, the dark path along the north edge of the yard, the corridor in front of the south classroom row and the pale aprons north and south of the maroon-roofed hall are hardscape. The dark roof inside the white-walled enclosure is unmapped and drawn as a roof. Canopy: the forest along the east edge, the belt along the south edge, the crowns west of the south row and north of the hall, the north canopy behind the north block and single crowns at the yard's edges. Registration: hand similarity fit to hand-picked OSM roof corners and junctions; independent check errors 1.27 m, 2.48 m, 2.47 m. Trunks sit inside their observed crowns; crowns may overhang roofs and roads. Complete mapped roofs, pitches, full-width paths/roads, water and farmland remain unchanged. Ground under opaque canopy is not invented. No surveyed boundary, species, construction date or exact inventory inferred; no bitmap ships."
